WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.930
Your next client won't ask you for an agent.

2
00:00:01.980 --> 00:00:03.510
They'll ask, where do I start?

3
00:00:03.848 --> 00:00:03.978
They’ll ask, “Where do I start?” And

4
00:00:03.978 --> 00:00:05.278
if you answer by talking about a

5
00:00:05.278 --> 00:00:06.238
tool, they’ll thank you,

6
00:00:06.238 --> 00:00:08.698
hang up, and ask ChatGPT instead.

7
00:00:08.698 --> 00:00:09.738
In this video,

8
00:00:09.738 --> 00:00:11.158
I want to show you what AI

9
00:00:11.158 --> 00:00:13.258
consulting looks like in practice and how

10
00:00:13.258 --> 00:00:14.258
to get ready to do this work

11
00:00:14.258 --> 00:00:15.458
in 2027.

12
00:00:15.458 --> 00:00:17.438
AI consulting isn’t selling tools.

13
00:00:17.438 --> 00:00:18.818
It isn’t building a chatbot.

14
00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:21.618
And it isn’t installing the latest agent.

15
00:00:21.618 --> 00:00:23.958
Consulting means stepping into the client’s business,

16
00:00:23.958 --> 00:00:25.898
finding the problem that’s really holding back

17
00:00:25.898 --> 00:00:28.318
results, and prescribing the simplest solution that

18
00:00:28.318 --> 00:00:28.838
fixes it.

19
00:00:28.838 --> 00:00:30.638
AI is your toolbox.

20
00:00:30.638 --> 00:00:31.998
It isn’t your job description.

21
00:00:31.998 --> 00:00:33.478
And in 2027,

22
00:00:33.478 --> 00:00:35.038
you’ll wear two hats.

23
00:00:35.038 --> 00:00:36.418
The consultant says what to do:

24
00:00:36.418 --> 00:00:37.898
which process to tackle first,

25
00:00:37.898 --> 00:00:38.838
what goes to a person,

26
00:00:38.838 --> 00:00:40.178
and what goes to an agent.

27
00:00:40.178 --> 00:00:41.618
The mentor helps the client do it

28
00:00:41.618 --> 00:00:42.138
on their own.

29
00:00:42.138 --> 00:00:43.658
Because clients will want to build their

30
00:00:43.658 --> 00:00:44.658
own AI projects.

31
00:00:44.658 --> 00:00:45.398
You can fight that,

32
00:00:45.398 --> 00:00:46.558
or you can be the person who

33
00:00:46.558 --> 00:00:47.778
helps them build the right way.

34
00:00:47.778 --> 00:00:49.798
The person who teaches becomes the go-to

35
00:00:49.798 --> 00:00:51.318
expert inside the company.

36
00:00:51.318 --> 00:00:52.758
So what does consulting look like in

37
00:00:52.758 --> 00:00:53.358
practice?

38
00:00:53.358 --> 00:00:54.398
Five steps.

39
00:00:54.398 --> 00:00:55.938
First: the conversation.

40
00:00:55.938 --> 00:00:56.918
Before any tool,

41
00:00:56.918 --> 00:00:57.658
ask questions.

42
00:00:57.658 --> 00:00:59.238
What takes up most of the team’s

43
00:00:59.238 --> 00:00:59.538
time?

44
00:00:59.538 --> 00:01:01.198
Where is the business losing money?

45
00:01:01.198 --> 00:01:02.798
Where do the most mistakes happen?

46
00:01:02.798 --> 00:01:03.858
Who decides what?

47
00:01:03.858 --> 00:01:05.698
Second: the one-page diagnosis.

48
00:01:05.698 --> 00:01:07.378
The process, the bottleneck,

49
00:01:07.378 --> 00:01:08.458
and four columns:

50
00:01:08.458 --> 00:01:09.618
this stays with a person,

51
00:01:09.618 --> 00:01:10.718
this goes to an agent,

52
00:01:10.718 --> 00:01:11.998
this is simple automation,

53
00:01:11.998 --> 00:01:13.798
and this should no longer exist.

54
00:01:13.798 --> 00:01:15.818
Third: the simplest solution.

55
00:01:15.818 --> 00:01:17.058
Start with the basics.

56
00:01:17.058 --> 00:01:19.038
If automation without AI solves it,

57
00:01:19.038 --> 00:01:21.258
great: it’s cheaper and more reliable.

58
00:01:21.258 --> 00:01:22.978
Use an agent only when the problem

59
00:01:22.978 --> 00:01:23.958
calls for one.

60
00:01:23.958 --> 00:01:25.238
Fourth: a small pilot,

61
00:01:25.238 --> 00:01:26.958
with success criteria agreed on before you

62
00:01:26.958 --> 00:01:27.178
start.

63
00:01:27.178 --> 00:01:29.618
That way, no one argues later about

64
00:01:29.618 --> 00:01:30.578
whether it worked.

65
00:01:30.578 --> 00:01:32.398
And fifth: teach and follow up.

66
00:01:32.398 --> 00:01:33.718
The team learns to use it,

67
00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:34.718
you measure the results,

68
00:01:34.718 --> 00:01:36.458
and you make adjustments month by month.

69
00:01:36.458 --> 00:01:37.758
That’s how you build a contract that

70
00:01:37.758 --> 00:01:38.818
doesn’t end at delivery.

71
00:01:38.818 --> 00:01:40.038
Here’s an example.

72
00:01:40.038 --> 00:01:42.258
A clinic says it’s losing appointments because

73
00:01:42.258 --> 00:01:43.318
patients don’t show up.

74
00:01:43.318 --> 00:01:44.878
The temptation is to sell a full-service

75
00:01:44.878 --> 00:01:45.318
agent.

76
00:01:45.318 --> 00:01:47.338
But the diagnosis shows something else:

77
00:01:47.338 --> 00:01:49.378
appointment reminders are simple automation.

78
00:01:49.378 --> 00:01:50.538
They don’t need an agent.

79
00:01:50.538 --> 00:01:51.918
The agent steps in to talk with

80
00:01:51.918 --> 00:01:53.318
patients who want to reschedule.

81
00:01:53.318 --> 00:01:55.098
And deciding whether to fit someone into

82
00:01:55.098 --> 00:01:57.178
the schedule stays with the front desk.

83
00:01:57.178 --> 00:01:58.918
Three pieces, each in the right place.

84
00:01:58.918 --> 00:01:59.918
That’s consulting.

85
00:01:59.918 --> 00:02:01.438
So how do you get ready?

86
00:02:01.438 --> 00:02:02.378
Five moves.

87
00:02:02.378 --> 00:02:04.398
One: choose an industry and learn how

88
00:02:04.398 --> 00:02:05.618
it makes and loses money.

89
00:02:05.618 --> 00:02:07.818
Two: do your first consulting project on

90
00:02:07.818 --> 00:02:09.418
yourself, or on a business you know.

91
00:02:09.418 --> 00:02:10.218
Do it for free,

92
00:02:10.218 --> 00:02:11.238
so you can learn.

93
00:02:11.238 --> 00:02:12.838
Three: build your toolkit.

94
00:02:12.838 --> 00:02:14.118
A list of questions,

95
00:02:14.118 --> 00:02:15.658
a one-page diagnosis template,

96
00:02:15.658 --> 00:02:17.578
and a proposal template.

97
00:02:17.898 --> 00:02:19.438
Four: learn agent management,

98
00:02:19.438 --> 00:02:21.458
because that’s what you’ll teach the client:

99
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:23.758
goals, context, limits on autonomy,

100
00:02:23.758 --> 00:02:25.638
evaluation, and supervision.

101
00:02:25.638 --> 00:02:27.538
And five: practice explaining all of this

102
00:02:27.538 --> 00:02:28.558
to nontechnical people.

103
00:02:28.558 --> 00:02:30.238
If the business owner doesn’t understand your

104
00:02:30.238 --> 00:02:31.618
diagnosis, they won’t buy.

105
00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:32.818
And avoid three mistakes.

106
00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:33.918
Starting with the tool.

107
00:02:33.918 --> 00:02:35.718
Promising results without agreeing on how to

108
00:02:35.718 --> 00:02:36.198
measure them.

109
00:02:36.198 --> 00:02:37.978
And doing everything for the client until

110
00:02:37.978 --> 00:02:39.378
they depend on you for everything.

111
00:02:39.378 --> 00:02:41.198
A good mentor makes the client stronger,

112
00:02:41.198 --> 00:02:42.198
not more dependent.

113
00:02:42.198 --> 00:02:43.138
To get started,

114
00:02:43.138 --> 00:02:45.118
we created the AI Consulting section in

115
00:02:45.118 --> 00:02:46.498
the INEMA events area.

116
00:02:46.498 --> 00:02:47.738
It has the four roles,

117
00:02:47.738 --> 00:02:49.318
the method, the AI Consultant course,

118
00:02:49.318 --> 00:02:50.698
the From Zero to Your First Client

119
00:02:50.698 --> 00:02:52.618
program, the Agent Management course,

120
00:02:52.618 --> 00:02:54.238
and open toolkits you can use with

121
00:02:54.238 --> 00:02:55.918
clients, like the Margin X-Ray,

122
00:02:55.918 --> 00:02:57.398
which shows in dollars where a business

123
00:02:57.398 --> 00:02:58.158
is losing money.

124
00:02:58.158 --> 00:02:59.538
It’s all open and free at INEMA

125
00:02:59.538 --> 00:03:00.118
dot club.

126
00:03:00.118 --> 00:03:01.378
In 2027,

127
00:03:01.378 --> 00:03:02.798
the client will have the same agent

128
00:03:02.798 --> 00:03:03.278
you do.

129
00:03:03.278 --> 00:03:04.978
What they won’t have is clarity.

130
00:03:04.978 --> 00:03:06.318
The person who shows up with the

131
00:03:06.318 --> 00:03:08.358
right questions, a one-page diagnosis,

132
00:03:08.358 --> 00:03:10.198
and the patience to teach becomes a

133
00:03:10.198 --> 00:03:10.658
partner.

134
00:03:10.658 --> 00:03:11.758
So start this week:

135
00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:12.758
choose a business,

136
00:03:12.758 --> 00:03:14.438
ask the questions from the conversation,

137
00:03:14.438 --> 00:03:16.178
and write the diagnosis on one page.

138
00:03:16.178 --> 00:03:17.858
That’s your first consulting assignment.

